Specifically, it seems that if you hit a tame pudding, there's a one
in 2 + max(luck, 0) chance that the clone will not be tame (makemon.c,
line 742).  Also, they may eventually go untame from abuse if you hit
them enough, although that is surprising hard to achieve (since new
clones will have their tameness reset to 5, and since the HP halving
means most of them will typically die in less than 5 hits unless you
let them heal in between).

You don't want to sac the ones that died while tame, but the rest are
fair game.  The easiest way to keep them apart is to name your initial
tame pudding and rename any untame clones.

Alternatively, you can just leave the pudding on the altar level and
go elsewhere until it goes untame.  That way you don't have to take
any luck penalty at all.

(BTW, it's surprisingly funny to have a mix of tame and untame
puddings on a level.  They _will_ fight each other, and the tame ones
will happily eat the corpses of their fallen brethren.  I guess it
really is a pudding-eat-pudding world out there.)

